  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.2.15 - Emulated double (WebGPU/WebGL, Dekker and Ozaki): exact 64-bit integer conversions, stores and rounding (Round/Floor/Ceiling/Truncate/%/IEEERemainder were per f32 component); large emulated-double kernels compile in seconds instead of hanging the GPU (branch-free emulation library, forward-only helper state machine); WebGL Ozaki error terms no longer folded or fused by D3D; Wasm Math.Round returned 0. WebGL loops compile in seconds (the loop guard is a uniform; a literal made D3D FXC analyse every loop - Autolykos2 521 s -> 0.6 s) and no longer stop at 100000 iterations; Autolykos2 dataset generation runs on WebGL (Blake2b round loop). Struct buffers with 64-bit fields, alignment padding or byte/short fields use the real C# layout on WebGL, WebGPU and Wasm (were tightly packed or widened; Wasm stores clobbered the next element); WebGL can read 64-bit struct fields. Sub-word SubViews at a non-4-byte offset read the right elements on WebGL and WebGPU. Fork 2.3.4: CUDA RoundToEven. See CHANGELOG.md.",
